[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Spinlocks
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-11-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-11-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock static definition
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to define and initialize a spinlock object
at compile time.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a low-level mutual exclusion primitive that can be used in
both thread and interrupt contexts to protect shared data.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-28

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-11-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock acquisition
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to acquire a spinlock that disables IRQs on
the current CPU and returns a key representing the IRQ state prior to locking, blocking
until the lock is available.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to enter a critical section that is safe against both
concurrent threads and interrupt handlers.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-28

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-11-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock try-acquire
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to attempt to acquire a spinlock without
blocking, returning a failure indication when the lock is not immediately available.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-28

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-11-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock release
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to release a previously acquired spinlock and
restore the IRQ state to the value captured at acquisition time.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-28

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-11-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Non-Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock nesting order
STATEMENT: >>>
Spinlocks shall be properly nested: each release shall correspond to the most recent
acquisition on the same CPU, using the key returned by that acquisition.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-28

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-11-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Non-Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock usable in ISR context
STATEMENT: >>>
Spinlock acquisition and release interfaces shall be usable from interrupt service
routine context.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-28
